{"format":1,"seq":252,"writes":[{"type":"document.change","id":2,"content":{"version":3,"kind":"delta","ops":[["p",["generation","message","content"],1,0,[{"type":"text","text":"I went through all 15 saved session threads in this repo and found eight places where global or project functions repeatedly failed or needed a follow-up call. I didn't change or commit anything; this comment is the whole deliverable. I can turn any item into an issue or PR.\n\n**What I looked at:** pi-action saves each thread under `refs/pi/threads/*` (#352–#379). Threads #352–#363 only used `bash`, so the useful sample is **214 `typescript` calls in #365–#379**. 36 of them failed. About 28 of those failures came from friction with the functions themselves, not from real test or code failures.\n\n## What didn't work well\n\n1. **`gh.api` cuts off large JSON responses, which then can't be parsed** (5 failed calls, plus a regex workaround that came back empty). Output is capped at 50 KB by default, so `JSON.parse(r.stdout)` fails with `unexpected token: 'web'` and similar (#372, #375, #376). I re-ran two of these calls and got the same result:\n   - `repos/cv/pi-action/compare/v2.5.1...v2.5.2`: 50,944 bytes, `truncated: true`, invalid JSON.\n   - `pulls?per_page=4`: 51,197 bytes, also invalid.\n\n   The suggested recovery doesn't help: `runtime.completedCalls` returns the same cut-off output (376#7 failed again the same way). The signature also misleads: `{ method, fields }` passed as the second argument gave `args must be an array of strings` (375#21).\n\n2. **The model guesses `gh.pr` and the hint points the wrong way** (3 failures: 370#8, 372#43, 375#6). The error says `Did you mean: pr, ci, gh?`, which points at the project namespace `pr`, not at `gh.prCreate`, `gh.prList`, `gh.prView` or `gh.prMerge`.\n\n3. **Typed `gh` and `git` functions get bypassed.**\n   - `execFile(\"gh\", [\"pr\", \"create\" | \"view\" | \"merge\"])` was used 16 times, even though typed versions exist. `gh.prView` returns raw stdout, so callers parse the JSON themselves anyway.\n   - `as any` casts hid a real mistake: `prList({ fields })` should have been `json`.\n   - There's no typed `git switch`, `checkout`, `branch`, `reset`, `pull`, `fetch`, `rev-parse` or `ls-remote`. Together they went through `execFile` about "}]],["a",["generation","message","content",0,"thinkingSignature"],""],["a",["generation","message","content",1,"text"],"35 times.\n\n4. **`delivery.commit({ push: true })` on protected `main`** (370#7, 376#9). Both times it failed, and the model then moved the commit to a branch, reset `main` and opened a PR by hand. 366#8 was a one-off push rejection that wor"]]}}]}